# homelab-node-exporter configuration.
#
# Space- and/or comma-separated IP address(es) or CIDR(s) of the
# monitoring host(s) allowed to scrape THIS host's Prometheus exporter
# ports (node_exporter :9100 and any other homelab exporter on this
# host). Used on package configure to generate
# /etc/nftables.d/10-homelab-metrics.nft. Defaults to the fleet
# monitoring host, prod-homelabvm69's service-plane address. Edit +
# `dpkg-reconfigure homelab-node-exporter` (or reinstall) to change.
#
# Until 2026-11-09 this defaulted to 10.50.2.63 (the pre-cutover ct19
# monitoring host), so every fleet node's drop-in names an address that
# no longer scrapes anything. Nothing broke because homelab-agent's
# fleet-trust baseline (10-homelab-fleet-trust.nft) accepts all of
# 10.50/10.45/10.20 anyway; this rule only matters on a host WITHOUT the
# agent. Existing hosts keep their file (seeded once) -- correct them with
# this value + dpkg-reconfigure if the agent is ever removed from one.
MONITORING_HOSTS="10.50.2.213"
